@startuml
title Shutdown — host-controlled flush before SDK disposal
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #425466
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Application host" as host
participant "Lifecycle + sink" as lifecycle #EDF5FF
participant "Host-owned OTel SDK\nand processors" as sdk #FFF1D6
participant "Exporter / transport" as exporter #FFF1D6
participant "Collector / backend" as backend

host -> lifecycle : phase(STOPPING) / Phase(Stopping)
lifecycle -> sdk : Emit application.lifecycle.phase_changed
sdk --> lifecycle
lifecycle --> host
host -> host : Complete application shutdown work\nKeep telemetry dependencies alive
host -> lifecycle : phase(STOPPED) / Phase(Stopped)
lifecycle -> sdk : Emit final phase event
sdk --> lifecycle
lifecycle --> host
note over host, lifecycle
  STOPPED is a declaration before process exit,
  not proof that the process has terminated.
end note

host -> sdk : Request bounded force flush
note over host, sdk
  Java: forceFlush().join(10, SECONDS).isSuccess()
  .NET: LoggerProvider.ForceFlush(10_000)
end note
sdk -> exporter : Flush pending batch, if configured
exporter -> backend : Attempt export
backend --> exporter : Response, failure or timeout
exporter --> sdk : Completion / failure
sdk --> host : SDK flush result or wait timeout
alt Unsuccessful flush or timeout
  host -> host : Apply host failure-reporting policy
else Flush completed
  note over host, backend : Flush completion is not a durable-delivery guarantee.
end
host -> sdk : Close / dispose provider or host services
sdk -> exporter : Shutdown / dispose transport
exporter --> sdk
sdk --> host
host -> host : Process exits

note over host, exporter
  Flush BEFORE disposing .NET services: the SDK may initialize its HTTP client lazily.
  The lifecycle library never owns SDK shutdown and adds no retries or delivery guarantees.
  Abrupt process termination may skip this entire sequence.
end note
@enduml
